## SECTION 0: ZERO-OMISSION ENTERPRISE DEVELOPMENT PROTOCOL

### NON-NEGOTIABLE PRINCIPLE

Assume that every change affects multiple layers of the system.
Never assume a module, entity, screen, API, workflow, or database object is isolated.
The burden of proof is on the implementation to demonstrate completeness.
No code may be generated until a completeness audit is performed.

---

### MANDATORY DISCOVERY PROCESS

For every request identify:

- Existing modules, pages, routes, forms, components, layouts
- Existing APIs, services, repositories
- Existing database tables, views, stored procedures, triggers
- Existing queues, schedulers, events, notifications
- Existing reports, dashboards, integrations
- Existing permissions, feature flags, configuration files, environment variables
- Existing tests, documentation

Read /docs/architecture/module-map.md first. Reuse before creating. Never duplicate.

---

### DATABASE RULES

Before creating tables, verify:

- Existing entity already exists (see /docs/database/entities.md)
- Existing relationship exists (see /docs/database/relationships.md)
- Existing lookup or reference data exists

Generate before coding:

- ERD delta
- Relationship Matrix update
- Migration Plan
- Rollback Plan

Never create orphan tables. Never create duplicate master data.

Always include: PK, FK, Indexes, Audit Fields (created_at, updated_at, created_by), Soft Delete (deleted_at), Status Tracking.

---

### UI RULES

Every module must include:

List View | Detail View | Create Form | Edit Form | Delete Flow | Search | Filters | Sorting | Export | Import | Audit History | Activity Timeline | Mobile Support | Accessibility

Never create partial modules.

---

### BUSINESS LOGIC RULES

Always identify:

- Business Rules, State Transitions, Approval Flow
- Escalation Flow, Exception Flow, Notifications
- Audit Requirements

Never implement CRUD-only logic. Implement complete business lifecycle.

---

### CROSS-MODULE IMPACT ANALYSIS

Before coding, evaluate impact on (see /docs/architecture/dependency-map.md):

Authentication | Authorization | Master Data | Transactions | Reports | Dashboards | Notifications | Integrations | Scheduled Jobs | Analytics | Search | Caching

Assume impact exists until disproven.

---

### SECURITY RULES

Read /docs/security/permissions.md and /docs/security/roles.md before any implementation.

Review: Authentication | Authorization | RBAC | Field Security | Record Security | Encryption | Audit Logging | OWASP Risks

Security review is mandatory.

---

### TESTING RULES

Generate coverage for:

Unit | Integration | API | UI | Workflow | Security | Permissions | Regression | End-to-End

Every requirement must have test coverage.

---

